<title>USA: US Treasury 2-yr note yld seen at 5.65 pct at sale.</title>
<headline>US Treasury 2-yr note yld seen at 5.65 pct at sale.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Treasury's auction of $18.25 billion in two-year notes on Tuesday is expected to produce a yield between 5.65 and 5.6550 percent, dealers said.</p>
<p>At 1230 EDT/1730 GMT, the two-year notes were quoted at 5.65 percent in when-issued trade. Demand for the securities was strong, said a trader at a primary dealership.</p>
<p>The bidding deadline for the notes is 1300 EDT/1800 GMT and results are expected around 1345 EDT/1845 GMT.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1676</p>
</text>
